@startuml VibeShield-Subsystem-Decomposition
' =====================================================================
'  VibeShield - Subsystem Decomposition (UML component diagram)
'  Reflects the RUNNING system on `main` (verified 2026-06-28), not the
'  planned design. Connections are labelled with the contract that
'  defines them - OpenAPI-first, so most are .yaml specs under /api.
'
'  Honest caveats (also called out in-diagram):
'   * Entry point is the nginx gateway / k8s Ingress - NOT the API service.
'   * Real auth = self-contained Spring Boot auth-service issuing HMAC JWTs
'     (docs/auth.md).
'   * The GenAI endpoint is a hand-written client, NOT in the OpenAPI spec.
'   * Scanner-service is stateless (no DB); only api & auth touch Postgres.
' =====================================================================

skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 75
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
top to bottom direction

' ---- Tier 0/1: client + single entry point --------------------------
actor "Vibecoder's\nbrowser" as Browser
component "nginx gateway / k8s Ingress\n<<single entry point>>" as GW

' ---- Tier 2: things the gateway routes to (SPA + provided REST) ------
component "Frontend SPA\nReact + Vite\n(Nginx static)" as FE
' One openapi.yaml contract (single source of truth) realised by BOTH the
' API and Auth services; the GenAI REST seam is separate and not in the spec.
' Path groups live on the GW->interface edges; resources live in the service
' boxes. (PlantUML hangs interface text as a label graphviz won't reserve
' space for, so two same-named circles side by side always collide - hence
' the merge into one.)
interface "openapi.yaml" as I_REST
interface "REST/JSON\nnot in OpenAPI" as I_GEN

' ---- Tier 3: the application services -------------------------------
package "Spring Boot server side  (3 microservices)" as SB {
  component "API service\nwebsites - scans - findings\nreports - rescan/comparison" as API
  component "Auth service\nregister - login - JWT\npassword reset" as AUTH
  component "Scanner service\n<<internal-only - stateless>>\nHTTPS / headers / files checks" as SCAN
}
component "GenAI service\nPython - FastAPI - LangChain\nfix-prompt generation" as GENAI

' Internal-only contract the API calls the Scanner over (not gateway-routed).
interface "scanner-internal.yaml\nPOST /scan" as I_SCAN

' ---- Tier 4: persistence + external systems -------------------------
database "PostgreSQL 16\n(single instance)" as DB {
  component "public schema\nwebsites - scans - findings" as PUB
  component "auth_service schema\nusers - reset tokens" as ASC
}
cloud "OpenAI API\n(cloud LLM, gpt-4o-mini)" as LLM
node  "Target website\n(the user's live site)" as TARGET

' ---- Provided REST interfaces (component offers the contract) -------
' Gateway-facing contracts sit on a rank BETWEEN the gateway and the services
' it routes to, so GW -> interface -> service flows straight down without
' piling up. SCAN provides the internal contract the API consumes.
I_REST -down- API
I_REST -down- AUTH
I_GEN  -down- GENAI
SCAN   -up-   I_SCAN

' ---- Routing: browser -> gateway -> providers (by URL path) ---------
Browser --> GW : HTTPS
GW --> FE     : " /  (serves SPA)"
GW --> I_REST : " /api, /api/v1/auth, /auth"
GW --> I_GEN  : " /langchain"

' ---- Internal / outbound dependencies -------------------------------
' No label on this one: the interface circle already names the contract, and
' a label here would land on the package border the edge crosses.
API   --> I_SCAN
API   --> PUB    : "JPA / JDBC"
AUTH  --> ASC    : "JPA / JDBC"
SCAN  --> TARGET : "HTTP probes"
GENAI --> LLM    : "HTTPS"

' Keep the SPA + the two interfaces on one rank in routing order.
FE -[hidden]right- I_REST
I_REST -[hidden]right- I_GEN

@enduml
